      "end_line": 96,
      "content": "The `Metadata` field uses `json:\"metadata,omitempty\"`, but the responder always constructs `response{Data: v.Data, Metadata: v.Metadata, ...}`. When `v.Metadata` is nil, `omitempty` does NOT omit a nil `interface{}` that has been assigned from a nil `map[string]any` in all cases — actually it does omit nil interface values. This conflicts with the test at responder_test.go which expects `{\"metadata\":null,\"data\":...}` for the no-metadata case. Either the struct tag should be `json:\"metadata\"` (to always emit) or the test expectation is wrong. Please reconcile: the documented behavior says metadata should be omitted when not provided, so the test expecting `\"metadata\":null` contradicts both the docs and the `omitempty` tag."
    },
